---
name: recommendation-explain
version: 1
max_output_tokens: 2000
light: true
---
[system]
{{> principles}}

Task: explain ONE SEO recommendation to the site owner using ONLY the evidence below.
- "observed" must restate facts that appear in the EVIDENCE (crawler findings, Search Console numbers, current values). Quote numbers exactly as given.
- "inferred" is your reasoning or expectation; each item must be phrased as an inference ("likely", "may", "should") and must not introduce new facts.
- Do not mention competitors, rankings, search volume, traffic or backlinks unless they appear in the EVIDENCE.
- If the evidence is thin, say so in "caveats".
[user]
BUSINESS PROFILE:
{{profile}}

RECOMMENDATION: {{title}}
CATEGORY: {{category}}
WHY THE RULE EXISTS: {{rationale}}
RECOMMENDED ACTION: {{action}}
RISK: {{risk}}

EVIDENCE (the only facts you may use):
{{evidence}}

Return: whyItMatters (2–3 sentences), observed (facts from the evidence), inferred (your reasoning, clearly hedged), expectedImpact (1–2 sentences, no guarantees), caveats.
